ohos-kernel-port is a derivative work. The original authorship belongs to the
projects listed under "Derived from" below. This file records them; it does not
attempt to reassign or supersede their copyright.

## Derived from

### ophub/kernel and ophub/amlogic-s9xxx-armbian

    https://github.com/ophub/kernel
    https://github.com/ophub/amlogic-s9xxx-armbian

    Copyright (C) 2021 ophub contributors
    Copyright (C) 2021 https://github.com/unifreq/openwrt_packit
    Copyright (C) 2023 https://github.com/unifreq/linux-5.10.y-rk35xx

    Licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 2.

The multi-kernel build, patch-application, configuration-merging and
CI-pipeline approach of this project originates here. See NOTICE for the
substantive list of changes.

### unifreq

    https://github.com/unifreq/linux-6.6.y
    https://github.com/unifreq/linux-5.10.y
    https://github.com/unifreq/linux-5.15.y
    https://github.com/unifreq/linux-6.1.y
    https://github.com/unifreq/linux-6.12.y
    https://github.com/unifreq/linux-6.18.y
    https://github.com/unifreq/linux-5.10.y-rk35xx
    https://github.com/unifreq/linux-6.1.y-rockchip

    Copyright (C) the respective kernel authors.

    Licensed under GPL-2.0 WITH Linux-syscall-note.

ophub's kernel source trees are maintained by unifreq, and this project carries
the same attribution for the `upstream-*` lanes in the lane matrix.

### Linux kernel authors

    https://github.com/torvalds/linux
    https://www.kernel.org

    Copyright (C) the Linux kernel authors.

    Licensed under GPL-2.0 WITH Linux-syscall-note.

For the full list of contributors to any kernel this project builds, see the
`CREDITS` file and the git history of the corresponding kernel source tree
recorded in each artifact's `MANIFEST.txt`. Those files are not reproduced
here.

